## Context

Ticket 0074 (PR #83) fixed `warning(s)` and `file(s)` pluralization but
the exit criterion was overbroad — `check.go:94` and `validate.go:326`
still emit `FAILED (%d error(s))`. Pre-existing, not introduced by #83.
Surfaced during verify-gate round 2 as follow-up material.

## Actions

1. `check.go` line ~94: replace `"FAILED (%d error(s))"` with inline plural
   (`"error"` / `"errors"`).
2. `validate.go` line ~326: same treatment for the FAILED line.

## Test

Extend `tests/test_check.sh`: 1 error → `"1 error"`; 2 errors → `"2 errors"`.
Use `grep -qF "FAILED (1 error)"` and `grep -qF "FAILED (2 errors)"`.

## Exit criteria

- `grep -n 'error(s)' tickets/tools/go/check.go tickets/tools/go/validate.go` returns no matches.
- `make test` passes.
